Open Vanilla 0052 (on top of 0051, the self-test): Boss Fights' ready raider. A character in Boss Fights has
nothing to set up: in the Gurubashi hangout, a few seconds after it arrives, the realm makes it ready, and
refreshes it after every run.

Owner, 2026-10-23: "Have instant level 60 with all action bars activated, enough things in bags, all gear sets,
custom talent sets immediately active as well."

- Level: a character below OpenVanilla.BossFights.Ready.Level (60) is raised to it; the class's spells
  (AutoLearn) and every weapon skill at its maximum (Warfront::Arena::MaxSkills, what a duelist gets).
- Bags: an empty bag slot gets OpenVanilla.BossFights.Ready.Bag (4500, Traveler's Backpack).
- Talents: the spec of the talent tree the character's role plays (Protection for a warrior tank, Holy for a
  priest healer, ...; BossFightsReadyLogic.h TreeFor) is made active with that tree's raid build. DualSpec's
  templates take raid builds (the playerbots' PvE premade specs, BossFightsReadyLogic.h RaidBuilds) instead of
  PvP builds for Boss Fights characters, so every spec never used gets one. A player's own choice is never
  overridden: Boss Fights picks only while the talents are a template's on a character with no spec of its own
  saved, or are still exactly what Boss Fights set last time (characters table bossfights_ready). A role change
  (".wnl wf bf role") picks again on those terms.
- Gear: every gear set of the class in the bags (Warfront's kits, Warfront::GiveGearSets, for anyone and not only
  on Duels), and the role's set worn (BossFightsReadyLogic.h PickKit) when the body is bare, or wears only gear-set
  pieces (the first time), or still wears the set Boss Fights put on. Anything else worn is the player's own.
- Consumables: topped up on arrival, after every run and each minute in the hangout:
  OpenVanilla.BossFights.Ready.Consumables (potions, flasks, elixirs, food, bandages), .Consumables.Mana (water,
  for mana users), .Consumables.<Class> (reagents, poisons) and a hunter's arrows or shells for the ranged weapon
  worn (.Ready.Ammo, 1000; set as the ammunition). All sell for nothing (bossfights_world.sql).
- Action bars, on the server (so the self-test can check them and they're right before any addon runs): the active
  spec's raid abilities on the main bar, the class's buffs, auras, forms and utility on the bottom left bar, every
  other class spell on the bottom right and side bars, the main bar on the stance and form bars; on empty buttons
  only. A body under 10 minutes old whose bars Boss Fights hasn't laid out yet is cleared first (only the realm's
  starter layout is there). The Boss Fights addon switches the four extra bars on (a client setting).
- Duels keeps its hands off raiders: its hangout no longer sets a character up as a duelist before Boss Fights has
  looked at it (BossFights::Pending), so a new raider never gets Duels' layout first. (The Duels addon does the
  same on the client: no PvP layout and no "best kit" for a raider.)
- Refresh after a run, back in the hangout: health and mana full, cooldowns reset, the run's world buffs gone.
- ".wnl wf bf ready": made ready first when in the hangout, then on the BF tag, key=value pairs (the self-test,
  0051, reads level, spent, free, sets, buttons and consumables by key):
    ready,level=60,spec=Protection,spent=51,free=0,sets=3,setsof=3,worn=warrior-fury-h,slots=61,buttons=64,
          consumables=13,wanted=13,missing=-,ok=1
  (spec: spaces as "_"; sets: gear sets whole in the bags or worn, of setsof; worn: the kit key worn whole, "own",
  "mixed" or "-"; slots: free bag slots; buttons: action buttons set; consumables: items at their count, of
  wanted; missing: the item ids short, ':' separated, or "-"; ok: 1 when ready) and a chat line. The same line
  goes to the addon when the realm makes a raider ready, and after every run.

Settings (all on by default while OpenVanilla.BossFights = 1): OpenVanilla.BossFights.Ready, .Ready.Talents,
.Ready.Gear, .Ready.Bars, .Ready.Level, .Ready.Bag, .Ready.Ammo, .Ready.Consumables[.Mana|.<Class>].
Playerbots are left alone. Pure rules and their tests: BossFightsReadyLogic.h, realm/bossfights/tests/test_ready.cpp.

